# Add boxes to the planner's collision world. They JOIN the world, they do
# not replace it: the boxes already there (the scene, any added before, the
# robot's layers) all stay. Calls are anonymous and accumulate; nothing here
# removes a box. Publishing std_msgs/Empty on /reset is the way back to the
# world loaded at boot, and a SetWorld push replaces the boxes added since.
#
# Refused whole, and the world before it stays: a frame that is not the
# planning frame, a name already in the world (reset first to re-add one), a
# non-unit orientation, a dim that is not a finite number > 0, or more boxes
# than the collision cache holds. Cylinders and spheres: send their
# bounding box (cuRobo v0.7.8 collides with boxes only).
string frame_id                 # the planning frame, arm_mount on RAMMP's robots
CollisionBox[] boxes
---
bool success
string message                  # the world it made, or why it was refused
